  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to COR-L23 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets COR-L23. This indicates a potential mechanism where Mollicellin N is involved in the signaling or regulatory processes that are mediated by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. Additionally, the presence of a shared target (3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid) between Mollicellin N and A704, which also targets COR-L23, further supports a common pathway. The integration of these findings suggests that Mollicellin N may influence COR-L23 through a biochemical interaction involving a shared intermediate, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The evidence does not explicitly establish a direct link between Mollicellin N and COR-L23, but the cumulative scores and the shared target suggest a plausible, indirect relationship that warrants further investigation.",
